#User Manual for CBWAE LOSO Quantum EEG Pipeline
1. Overview

This project implements a LOSO (Leave-One-Subject-Out) EEG classification pipeline with:

Classical machine learning: Logistic Regression, Random Forest, kNN, SVM, XGBoost

Meta-learning: A neural network stacking ensemble using predictions and entropy measures

Quantum-inspired feature augmentation: Adds complex-valued features inspired by quantum mechanics

Advanced evaluation metrics: F1, Accuracy, Balanced Accuracy, MCC, Kappa, LogLoss, Brier score, ECE, confidence gap, uncertainty correlation

The main goal is to classify EEG signals (e.g., motor imagery) with high accuracy across subjects.

2. Scripts
A. EDF Presence Checker Script

Purpose:

Quickly checks if all your expected EDF files are present in a folder.

Supports file naming convention S###R04.edf and S###R06.edf (e.g., S001R04.edf).

Usage:

data_path = "/content"  # Change to your EDF folder


Runs through subjects S001 to S100 and prints missing files.

Recommendation:

Always run this first to ensure you have all necessary data before executing the main pipeline.

Useful if you have many subjects or suspect missing/corrupted files.

B. CBWAE LOSO Quantum Script (cbwae_novel_loso_quantum.py)

Purpose:

Performs full EEG classification using a multi-stage ensemble.

Supports feature extraction (time-domain, bandpower, wavelets).

Adds quantum-inspired feature augmentation.

Trains multiple base models, combines predictions with meta-learning DNN.

Provides per-subject results CSV and a summary report.

Key Features & Parameters:

Component	Description	User Options
DATA_ROOT	Root folder to search for EDF files	Change to your data path
WINDOW_SECONDS	Length of EEG segments (default 2s)	Adjust if different windowing needed
INCLUDE_WAVELET	Include wavelet features	True/False
N_SPLITS_OOF	Out-of-fold splits for base models	3–5 recommended
META_EPOCHS, META_BATCH	Meta-learning DNN training	Adjust for speed/accuracy tradeoff
QF_DIM	Dimension of quantum-inspired features	Default 32
CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD	For pseudo-labeling / novelty detection	Default 0.75

Outputs:

cbwae_loso_results.csv → metrics per subject

cbwae_loso_summary.txt → mean ± std summary across all subjects

3. Workflow / How to Use
Step 1: Verify EDF files

Run the EDF checker script to identify missing files.

Ensure all S###R04 and S###R06 pairs exist.

Step 2: Run main LOSO pipeline

Ensure all dependencies are installed (mne, scikit-learn, tensorflow, xgboost, pywt).

Run:

python cbwae_novel_loso_quantum.py


Monitor output per subject.

Step 3: Review results

Check CSV for per-subject accuracy and metrics.

Check summary file for mean ± std across all subjects.

4. Which Components to Use / Recommendations

Always:

EDF presence checker → ensures you won’t waste time.

Main LOSO pipeline → full evaluation.

Selective / Optional:

Quantum-inspired features (QF_DIM) → can be turned off by not stacking them if you want simpler classical ML evaluation.

Wavelet features → optional if computational resources are limited.

Meta-learning DNN → can skip and rely on weighted or best single model if you just need baseline performance.

Recommended Approach for New Users:

Step 1: EDF checker → ensure complete dataset

Step 2: Run full LOSO with quantum + meta-learning for best performance

Step 3: Optionally, turn off wavelet or quantum features to compare effect on accuracy

5. Notes / Tips

Computation: LOSO with meta-DNN can be slow if many subjects or windows. Use smaller META_EPOCHS for testing.

Randomness: Seed is fixed for reproducibility (RNG=42).

Missing Channels: The script expects EEG channels. If missing, it will raise an error.

File naming: Must match S###R04.edf / S###R06.edf convention.

